WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.794 --> 00:00:05.839
London, 1983.

00:00:07.757 --> 00:00:08.717
Good afternoon to you.

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:10.927
Well, it's decidedly parky
to say the least.

00:00:11.011 --> 00:00:14.305
And, in fact, it's not gonna get
any warmer, really, in the next few days

00:00:14.389 --> 00:00:16.975
because we're going to keep
these north to northeasterly…

00:00:17.058 --> 00:00:22.272
[McCusker] I certainly remember the day
because it was cold and miserable outside,

00:00:22.355 --> 00:00:24.399
and I was sitting in my office

00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:27.569
when a colleague of mine told me

00:00:27.652 --> 00:00:30.321
that he had been called
to Cranley Gardens,

00:00:30.822 --> 00:00:35.702
where suspected human remains
were pulled out of a manhole there.

00:00:45.754 --> 00:00:49.257
When we got there, the tenants
were standing around the manhole.

00:00:49.966 --> 00:00:51.760
The toilets had been blocked,

00:00:51.843 --> 00:00:55.889
and an engineer had been called
to clear the drains,

00:00:56.473 --> 00:01:00.351
and he discovered
huge amounts of flesh and bone.

00:01:00.935 --> 00:01:02.479
I have a limited knowledge,

00:01:02.562 --> 00:01:05.065
but very heavily suspected

00:01:05.148 --> 00:01:08.359
that it wasn't, um, animal, shall we say.

00:01:08.443 --> 00:01:11.488
[interviewer] Did anyone express
any particular interest in what you found?

00:01:11.571 --> 00:01:15.241
Yes. The guy, I believe,
was living in the top-floor flat.

00:01:19.662 --> 00:01:22.373
[McCusker] Then the tenants told me
that the previous evening,

00:01:22.457 --> 00:01:23.833
around about midnight,

00:01:24.417 --> 00:01:26.795
they had heard a scraping noise outside.

00:01:26.878 --> 00:01:29.339
When they went to the front door
and opened it,

00:01:29.422 --> 00:01:31.508
they saw the man from the upstairs flat.

00:01:32.092 --> 00:01:34.594
He was dressed in just a simple vest.

00:01:34.677 --> 00:01:37.847
And bearing in mind,
this was February, freezing cold.

00:01:37.931 --> 00:01:39.849
And they asked him if he was all right.

00:01:40.350 --> 00:01:43.269
And he said,
"I am. I've just been outside for a pee."

00:01:45.563 --> 00:01:47.982
I made further inquiries
at Cranley Gardens

00:01:48.066 --> 00:01:52.362
and found out he was
at the local&nbsp;Jobcentre where he worked.

00:02:00.745 --> 00:02:03.039
And he normally returned from his work

00:02:03.123 --> 00:02:05.250
at half past five every evening.

00:02:09.462 --> 00:02:13.341
We then found out
that the pieces of bones from the drains

00:02:13.883 --> 00:02:16.553
were indeed from a human body.

00:02:16.636 --> 00:02:19.472
And the pathologist said
that the piece of flesh

00:02:19.556 --> 00:02:22.475
appeared to have
strangulation marks on it.

00:02:22.559 --> 00:02:24.561
[tense suspenseful music playing]

00:02:27.063 --> 00:02:28.565
[McCusker] And lo and behold,

00:02:28.648 --> 00:02:30.775
we saw a man walking up the road.

00:02:35.989 --> 00:02:39.033
[Nilsen, singing]
♪ Oh, the time is coming ♪

00:02:39.701 --> 00:02:42.120
♪ The time is coming! ♪

00:02:43.037 --> 00:02:45.081
He was very calm indeed.

00:02:49.586 --> 00:02:52.088
[Nilsen] When I arrived
to Cranley Gardens,

00:02:52.172 --> 00:02:54.549
the police were unsure of their ground.

00:02:55.842 --> 00:03:00.305
They were fishing tentatively
in the hope of gaining information

00:03:00.388 --> 00:03:04.267
concerning the samples of human flesh
found down the house…

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:05.435
…drains.

00:03:06.436 --> 00:03:09.731
Nilsen then said, "Very strange
that police officers should come

00:03:09.814 --> 00:03:11.482
and talk to me about my drains."

00:03:11.566 --> 00:03:12.734
[camera shutter clicks]

00:03:13.610 --> 00:03:15.612
[McCusker] But he let us into the house…

00:03:15.695 --> 00:03:16.863
[camera shutter clicks]

00:03:16.946 --> 00:03:19.157
[McCusker]
…and we went up to the attic flat.

00:03:20.408 --> 00:03:21.826
[camera shutter clicks]

00:03:21.910 --> 00:03:24.204
[McCusker] And as soon
as he opened the door,

00:03:25.163 --> 00:03:26.873
the smell just came at you.

00:03:27.749 --> 00:03:29.000
[camera shutter clicks]

00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:32.128
[camera shutter clicks]

00:03:33.713 --> 00:03:36.382
-[camera shutter clicks]
-[McCusker] I knew that awful smell.

00:03:36.883 --> 00:03:38.426
So we said to him…

00:03:38.509 --> 00:03:42.305
[Nilsen overlaps] "Stop messing about.
Where's the rest of the body?"

00:03:42.889 --> 00:03:44.140
And he looked at me,

00:03:44.224 --> 00:03:45.767
and he pointed

00:03:46.768 --> 00:03:48.019
to the wardrobe.

